{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794232835,"nonce":"MxYn8V/Dg77OB9vEBdpYd0bdXQY=","title":"Every style pass tests each node against every rule: index rules by their subject","message":"The stylesheet passes (`apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree`,\n`apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides_for_subtree`, the state pass,\n`matching_base_rules`, `matching_animation` and the rest; 16 callers of\n`complex_rules()`) loop over the whole rule list and run\n`complex_selector_matches` per node. Only a rule that is a single bare class\ntakes the class index; cn's rules are mostly compounds\n(`.cn-x[data-state=..]`, `.a .b`), so they all take the slow path. With\nCN_STYLES loaded, any rebuilt subtree is matched against all of it.\n\nMeasured on the russl toy (release, headless): a keystroke in the editor\ncosts ~11 ms, and a `sample` over 4000 keystrokes puts the largest share in\n`has_class`, `compound_matches`, `complex_selector_matches` and the sip\nhasher, under `process_pending_subtree_rebuilds_routed` →\n`apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree` / `..._layout_overrides_for_subtree`,\nand under the state pass. The toy's editor rebuild is the subtree here; the\nsame cost lands on every full build and every Stateful rebuild.\n\nFix, as browsers do: index each rule by its subject compound's key, the\nmost selective of id, class, attribute name, or element type, with a\nuniversal bucket. A node's candidates are the union of its id's, classes',\nattribute names' and type's buckets plus the universal one; only those run\nthe full match, in cascade order. Build the index once per stylesheet\n(it changes on reparse), and route every pass through one\n`candidate_rules(node)`.\n\nRelated: the code editor's full rebuild per change (52a49d0) multiplies\nthis cost by the document size.","files":null}]}